  "details": "I've brought up this issue with support, and was linked by someone to here. It looks like others have had similar issues, but it hasn't been brought up for a few months.\n\nBasically, the Vive's trackpads are very fragile, and worn out quickly by repetitive clicking, which is the only way to move in VRChat. After 30 hours of playing, my trackpads have become noticeably more \"squishy\" rather than crisp.\n\nThe simple solution: adjust the current locomotion or add a new option to initiate locomotion through touch, rather than clicking and dragging. You'd have to click the menu button before you can move, and the actual menu can be opened with the opposite hand.\n\nVive controllers are $100+, and HTC's repair service is questionable at best. If the trackpad breaks, you're stuck with opening the controller and fixing it yourself, which is a pain in the rear if it's just a single game that breaks your controllers.",
